  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEF III Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Fund is expected to increase access to early-stage venture capital and provide operational support for technology startups in Turkiye and CEE, potentially resulting in business growth. The project is also expected to strengthen market integration in the real and financial sector in Turkiye and CEE, through the expansion of investees with disruptive business models, via demonstration and replication and/or innovation channels. Moreover, the project will strengthen the digital entrepreneurship ecosystem in the target regions, through inducing further investment by venture capital funds and establishment of local digital ventures, via demonstration and replication channels.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project consists of an IFC equity commitment of up to $25 million with a co-investment envelope of $15 million in Digital East Fund III, SCSp (the Fund, or Fund III or DEF III), a venture capital (VC) fund that will invest in technology companies in Turkiye and Central Eastern Europe (CEE).</narrative>
  </description>
